import{_ as o,o as t,c as a,a2 as r}from"./chunks/framework.BN3Eol-0.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"UXD-015 — Layer chips are one flat horizontal row on Explore and every world, and the INDEX absorbs the A–Z","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-015-flat-chip-row.md","filePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-015-flat-chip-row.md"}'),s={name:"uxs/decisions/UXD-015-flat-chip-row.md"};function n(i,e,d,l,c,h){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<h1 id="uxd-015-—-layer-chips-are-one-flat-horizontal-row-on-explore-and-every-world-and-the-index-absorbs-the-a–z" tabindex="-1">UXD-015 — Layer chips are one flat horizontal row on Explore and every world, and the INDEX absorbs the A–Z <a class="header-anchor" href="#uxd-015-—-layer-chips-are-one-flat-horizontal-row-on-explore-and-every-world-and-the-index-absorbs-the-a–z" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;UXD-015 — Layer chips are one flat horizontal row on Explore and every world, and the INDEX absorbs the A–Z&quot;">​</a></h1><ul><li><strong>Status</strong>: accepted</li><li><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-11-12 (proposed and decided)</li><li><strong>Decider</strong>: the operator, 2026-11-12 — flat row on every world, Earth&#39;s two master switches dropped (&quot;A4/A5 follow-up&quot;, &quot;A3–A6 answers&quot;, &quot;A5 last two&quot;), then ONE ORBITERS chip on Earth and OBSERVATORIES for the ground telescopes (&quot;A4–A6 open items&quot;: &quot;1 sync all orbiters to listen 1 chip, 2a, 3a, 4a, 5a&quot;), and &quot;basically we absorb A–Z into index&quot; (&quot;L20 / L25 / L28 and the A–Z&quot;; <code>docs/wip/2026-11-11-ux-feedback-plan.md</code>); then one HUD row with a fixed RESET VIEW slot (&quot;One HUD row&quot;, same file, 2026-11-12). Inputs: C2, W7, plan Q5</li><li><strong>Answers</strong>: C2, W7; slice A5</li><li><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>src/lib/components/LayerChipRow.svelte</code>, <code>src/lib/surface-scene/SurfaceScene.svelte</code>, <code>SurfaceIndexPanel.svelte</code>, <code>src/lib/components/ExploreBodyIndex.svelte</code> (since replaced by <code>ScaleIndex.svelte</code>, <a href="./UXD-017-one-index-on-every-scale">UXD-017</a>), <code>EntityIndex.svelte</code>, <code>src/routes/explore/HudControls.svelte</code>, <code>src/routes/explore/+page.svelte</code> (ruler constants), <code>src/routes/{moon,mars,venus}/+page.svelte</code>; messages (two keys added, 15 removed, one renamed); <code>scripts/i18n-tools/native-terms.json</code> (<code>observatory</code>); <a href="./../IA">IA §controls</a>; Design System §5.7 (<code>docs/concept/05_Design_System.md</code>); AGENTS.md &quot;Design system&quot; block; <code>docs/adr/TA.md</code>; <a href="./../../adr/ADR-096">ADR-096</a> item 11; <code>src/lib/components/README.md</code>; <code>src/lib/surface-scene/README.md</code></li></ul><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><p>At <code>81e0d43c0dd</code> Earth showed its layers as a column of 10 items with two full-row headers (ON EARTH / IN SPACE) that were master switches, reaching about 534 px down and into the orbit ruler on short windows, with two chips both labelled TELESCOPES; Moon, Mars and Venus showed flat lists; Explore had five inline chips. The four scene routes (/moon /mars /venus /explore) also carried a floating A–Z tab beside the INDEX pull tab: two index affordances for the same objects.</p><h2 id="options" tabindex="-1">Options <a class="header-anchor" href="#options" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Options&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Group every world (ON GROUND / IN SPACE). 2. Flatten Earth and every world. 3. Two stacked rows. For the Earth row: keep four category chips under ORBITERS, or one ORBITERS chip like the other worlds. For the A–Z: keep the tab, or put the links into the INDEX.</li></ol><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Option 2: one flat horizontal row of chips on Explore and every world, from one component (<code>LayerChipRow</code>), wrapping between chips where the width runs out; no captions, no groups, no master switches, no greyed chip. Earth&#39;s row is SURFACE · AUTO, LAUNCHPADS, MUSEUMS, OBSERVATORIES, ORBITERS: one ORBITERS chip switches every orbiter (stations, space telescopes, constellations, comsats and the Moon orbiters), as on Moon, Mars and Venus; the four category chips and both masters are gone. The ground telescopes chip is OBSERVATORIES (<code>observatory</code> is in the glossary first, 13 locales). The chip look is <a href="./UXD-014-one-chip-and-filter">UXD-014</a>.</p><p>The INDEX absorbs the A–Z. On /moon, /mars, /venus and /explore each INDEX row whose object has an entity page also carries a real link to it, and the separate A–Z tab is removed. The INDEX panel is always in the DOM (hidden while closed) and, before the sites load, is the plain list of every entity page from the route&#39;s server load, so the prerendered HTML links every page of the hub (<a href="./../../adr/ADR-096">ADR-096</a> item 11 still holds). <code>/missions</code> and <code>/fleet</code> have no INDEX panel and keep the A–Z at the page foot.</p><p>One HUD row (fine pointer, Explore and every world). The view actions (2D, RESET VIEW, SPIN, AR, SKY where present) and the layer chips are one row: the actions group first, a 12 px gap (no line, no caption), then the layer group. Two inline groups: when the row does not fit it wraps between the groups (the layer group moves to the next line as a block and wraps inside itself only if it alone is too wide), never leaving one action chip alone on a line. With a detail panel open the whole row stops before it (<code>hud-beside-panel</code>; any open panel counts: site, orbiter, museum, observatory). Touch is unchanged: the layers live in the LAYERS drawer and the top cluster is actions only. RESET VIEW is always rendered in its slot, and so is SPIN on the worlds: disabled (the A4 disabled look) when there is nothing to reset or the view is 2D, never unmounted, so no chip shifts as the view changes. AR and SKY mount once their availability resolves on mount and are absent where the device cannot run them (every fine pointer), so they never appear or vanish after first paint.</p><p><strong>Amendment 2026-11-23 (operator, mobile audit).</strong> On touch the Worlds&#39; LAYERS and NATIONS drawers list their toggles as rows in the orbit ruler&#39;s look (<code>DrawerToggleRows</code>: dot, name, lit band when on; same ids and order as the HUD chips), in a panel as wide as its rows rather than the full width, and the Worlds&#39; drawers carry no ×: the open tab closes its panel (Esc, a tap on the dimmed scene and a swipe down still do). The 44 px chips read oversized in a panel the HUD opened. The same day /explore took the same pattern: its CONTROLS drawer lists the layers as rows, the RULER and CONTROLS panels are as wide as their rows, and no drawer carries a ×; the scale ladder is compact rows too. The fine-pointer HUD row is unchanged.</p><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Consequences&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The layer block drops from about 420 px of column to 30–66 px of row; the chip-driven ruler shift and the Explore ruler offsets (376 / 196 px) are deleted; the object-index panel starts under the measured HUD bottom; Earth&#39;s sub-chips are independent toggles and the Moon orbiters on Earth ride the one ORBITERS chip; Earth&#39;s per-category visibility state and <code>categoryDefaultVisible</code> are removed; the worlds&#39; HUD baselines regenerate once with A4. Explore&#39;s chip row is <code>LayerChipRow</code>, and its PATHS chip carries <code>data-audio-stage</code> through the config <code>attrs</code>. The footer stays compact below 1450 px on the four scene routes (it was set for the A–Z tab; whether /moon /mars /venus still need it is not measured). (Corrected 2026-11-12: the stars of the /explore neighbourhood INDEX do have entity pages, <code>/explore/stars/&lt;id&gt;</code> since ADR-096 items 13–14, and carry the <code>↗</code> link like every other row with a page.) The worlds&#39; INDEX pull tab moves up out of the way of the imagery card, the locate chip and the orbit ruler (it measures them); on /explore the ruler sits right of the tab (<code>--ruler-left</code> 44 px).</p><h2 id="verification" tabindex="-1">Verification <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>tests/e2e/chip-row.spec.ts</code> (membership, order, no group or disabled layer chip, no column, actions and layers in one band with a 12 px gap, the row stops before every kind of open panel, no chip shifts on select / reset on /explore /mars /moon), <code>tests/e2e/index-links.spec.ts</code> (prerendered links to every entity page of each hub in en and de, rows carry links, no floating A–Z) and <code>tests/e2e/footer-dock.spec.ts</code> (no two world HUD parts intersect, INDEX panel closed and open) on three projects; <code>a5-check.py</code> prints <code>A5-CHECK violations: 0</code>.</p>',15)])])}const w=o(s,[["render",n]]);export{u as __pageData,w as default};
